{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/434541-ideas-on-breaking-tribal-vows","id":434541,"title":"Ideas on breaking Tribal Vows","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-09T14:26:22-07:00","id":434541,"title":"Ideas on breaking Tribal Vows","content":"So my Bale Hounds chronicle going to end - and before the great finale, I want to do something big: <b>I want to test the Tribal Vows of PCs, how much they <i>really </i>embodied their Firstborns.</b><br /> <br /> I have some rough ideas for this, but I thought general topic on this could serve also other <b>Werewolf</b> Storytellers. <br /> <br /> Quick reminder about what, precisely, we talk about here:<ul><li><b>Blood Talons</b> - <i>Offer No Surrender You Would Not Accept</i></li> <li><b>Bone Shadows</b> - <i>Pay Each Spirit in Kind</i></li> <li><b>Hunters in Darkness</b> -<i> Let No Sacred Place in Your Territory Be Violated</i></li> <li><b>Iron Masters</b><i> - </i> <i>Honor Your Territory in All Things</i></li> <li><b>Storm Lords</b> - <i>Allow No One to Witness or to Tend Your Weakness</i></li> </ul>So, let's look for how characters can be made in to breaking their Vows... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, <b>how many times the Firstborn could forgive violation of his Vow?</b><br /> <br /> P.S. About the mechanics of Harmony Breaking Points by Tribal Vows breaking we talk about in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/432917-so-sinning-in-2nd-ed?p=433929#post433929\">this topic</a>. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T14:51:35-07:00","id":434607,"title":"","content":"Blood Talons: Do something particularly heinous if your enemy gives up. If your enemy begs for his life like a coward, screwing over his pack in the process, destroy the pack. When karma comes to get you, act just as the enemy did, and be not one bit sorry about it. Make sure what the character causes is as heartbreaking and gut-wrenching as possible.<br /> <br /> Bone Shadows: If a spirit makes a great sacrifice for your pack, do not honour it. Spit in the spirit's face, and show it such gross disrespect that your pack balks at you. A particularly loathsome spirit that, nonetheless, held its promise and helped you in the end could help achieve this.<br /> <br /> Hunters In Darkness: Something has to happen to the most sacred part of your turf, and it has to be BAD. We're talking Ashwood-Abbey-Violating-A-Locus-And-Making-It-A-Wound bad. Enough said.<br /> <br /> Iron Masters: Compromise your territory in a huge way. Dishonour it somehow, such as giving up a chunk of an environmentally-vulnerable part that has wolves living in it just because it means the Bale Hounds might spare you. Give into the temptation to pawn it off despite all it's done for you.<br /> <br /> Storm Lords: Be an absolute coward. Show you're nothing but the submit-and-roll-over type. Make such a disgusting fool of yourself, no one would consider you a sane or effective leader.<br /> <br /> <br /> These acts should probably be enough, in and of themselves, to get the Firstborn mad at you reaaaaally quickly. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T15:05:21-07:00","id":434624,"title":"","content":"More I was thinking about making PCs in to &quot;Breaking the Vow&quot; trap. Like how Bale Hounds should manipulate Blood Talon player, so he <i>would offer surrender he would not accept</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T15:06:50-07:00","id":434630,"title":"","content":"For the Hunter in Darkness, I think it's important to make sure the violation is unambiguously the character's fault. They don't have to be the one who does the violating, but it should be something that was in the character's power to prevent, and they chose not to. Otherwise they're just the victim. If their territory just gets attacked by something they would have no hope to defend against - if they give it their all and still fail to protect their territory - there's nothing for them to feel guilty about. Even if Black Wolf holds them responsible, they might still feel justified in having done their best against impossible odds. Instead, if you really want to strike a low blow, make sure it's something they could easily stop, but give them a compelling reason not to stop it. The classic super villain sadistic choice moment. Do you just let [insert thing the character cares deeply about] die? Or do you break your oath and allow your territory to be violated in order to save [important thing]?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T15:09:35-07:00","id":434634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/434541-ideas-on-breaking-tribal-vows?p=434624#post434624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More I was thinking about making PCs in to &quot;Breaking the Vow&quot; trap. Like how Bale Hounds should manipulate Blood Talon player, so he <i>would offer surrender he would not accept</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bale Hounds torture Lunes until they snap. If they somehow presented the BT player a situation that would break him in half emotionally, mentally and spiritually, via using a situation where he'd almost never give up, that would probably do it. If Blood Talons are the &quot;proud warrior&quot; tribe, then the best way to break them is to beat that pride out of them.<br /> <br /> Edit: Charlaquin ninja-posted me, haha. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Basically, what he/she/ze said, only apply it to the Talons as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T15:32:48-07:00","id":434729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/434541-ideas-on-breaking-tribal-vows?p=434624#post434624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More I was thinking about making PCs in to &quot;Breaking the Vow&quot; trap. Like how Bale Hounds should manipulate Blood Talon player, so he <i>would offer surrender he would not accept</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Make breaking the vow easier and way more desirable than not breaking it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood Talons: Do something particularly heinous if your enemy gives up. If your enemy begs for his life like a coward, screwing over his pack in the process, destroy the pack. When karma comes to get you, act just as the enemy did, and be not one bit sorry about it. Make sure what the character causes is as heartbreaking and gut-wrenching as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have the Bale Hound surrender and ask to repent after doing something rather horrible. Killing their family, murdering a pack member, burning their mint collection of Vampire: The Eternal Struggle cards. Leave everything open to the Blood Talon, give him every opportunity for revenge or pay back.<br /> <br /> Classic super villain morality or Moriarty trick. Make it so easy to punish and torture or maim the Bale Hound.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bone Shadows: If a spirit makes a great sacrifice for your pack, do not honour it. Spit in the spirit's face, and show it such gross disrespect that your pack balks at you. A particularly loathsome spirit that, nonetheless, held its promise and helped you in the end could help achieve this.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to trick the Bone Shadow. What one Spirit thinks of as respect another thinks of as a dishonour. Make sure again, its really easy or desirable to accomplish, like stepping into the forbidden stream or 'touch nothing but the lamp.'<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunters In Darkness: Something has to happen to the most sacred part of your turf, and it has to be BAD. We're talking Ashwood-Abbey-Violating-A-Locus-And-Making-It-A-Wound bad. Enough said.</div> </div> </div> </div>Give them a choice between the stick and the carrot and take it a step further. Make it their home. Their family. Their school or their work. Make it really personal or horrifically bad.<br /> <br /> Depending on the character you'll have to choose between which to use, carrot or stick. The really good thing they want or need, or the really bad thing they never want to have happen. They get the good thing or prevent the bad thing at the cost of their sacred place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iron Masters: Compromise your territory in a huge way. Dishonour it somehow, such as giving up a chunk of an environmentally-vulnerable part that has wolves living in it just because it means the Bale Hounds might spare you. Give into the temptation to pawn it off despite all it's done for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one can be the same as the Hunters in Darkness but framed in the sense of gain or loss in value of territory.<br /> <br /> You can also trick them into violating their territory, make them think they're going to cleanse the resonance of that locus, or kill the spirit/person/host that sets everything right. Really their tipping the balance further to the wrong side.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Storm Lords: Be an absolute coward. Show you're nothing but the submit-and-roll-over type. Make such a disgusting fool of yourself, no one would consider you a sane or effective leader.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll usually have to use the stick on this one, something that they really can't give up, something so damning they have to shame themselves or something worth shaming themselves completely for, like the lives of their pack. Repeat it multiple times. Make them submit to your will and give them empty promises as you go further and further until they can't take it anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","user":"GilboD","date":". 03-09-2015, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T15:35:16-07:00","id":434730,"title":"","content":"Well, the classic way to do this is to involve NPCs the character really cares about or<br /> <br /> Blood Talon: You have to offer him a surrender you would not accept. The alternative is killing him.<br /> Bone Shadow: Paying this spirit in kind would cause more problems than it would solve and endanger people you care about.<br /> Hunters in Darkness: The one doing the violating is someone you care about.<br /> Iron Masters: Ditto.<br /> Storm Lords: Well, this one's easy.<br /> <br /> <br /> That all being said, trying to build elaborate scenarios that end with a character having to break their Vow reeks a bit of desperately trying to make the Paladin Fall in D&amp;D, so should be done with the utmost circumspection.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T18:24:18-07:00","id":434990,"title":"","content":"With the Hunters in Darkness you could do something particularly interesting. Simply by forcing them to stick to their vow they could ruin the sanctity of their sacred place, or twist it into something awful. Throw a rave there, assemble flash zombie mobs and other gatherings of people. The Hunter will have to do something, but if they don't think it through they could taint the place.<br /> <br /> The Iron Masters could also be susceptible to a more long-term shift in dynamics. You could take cues from Pentex here, where their territory is corrupted but as a natural course of things. Businesses get bought out, mom and pop stores are bulldozed for big box stores, sweatshops open up and the police assigned to the place are ordered to look the other way at most offenses. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=phWcmwlpjQo\" target=\"_blank\">How do you honor your territory when it has become a shallow thing leeching life and respect from everyone within?</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-09-2015, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T18:40:52-07:00","id":435007,"title":"","content":"Does the blood Talon have a lover? Make it a closet betrayel. She knew the locus location and gave it away? She gave in to the predators animal magnetism? Make it not only a breaking point moment, but something that risks basu-I'm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T00:07:14-07:00","id":435402,"title":"","content":"Thanks for general ideas, I surely use them in next game I will run!<br /> <br /> The problem is in now game takes place in small town, and PCs are not integrated even to them. The Forsaken pack is living - literally - in the woods ( and mountains ) and still fight to free the Wounds spirits possessing citizens. Beside the Bale Hounds and PCs pack, there is only PCs mentor/ alpha's lover ex-Bale Hound, but she is missing now ( probably kidnapped by the Hounds ).<br /> <br /> But there is ex-PC Elodoth character I taken few games days before out of action. I think that she could be now confused and scared, and Bale Hounds Elodoth will get her, use Auspice Benefit - and lead her in to the Death Rage where she will find new life clarity. And this is how she could become Hound of Rage then.<br /> <br /> I was planing to return to her to her old pack as double agent that will try to play on PCs Tribal Vows, shown them how &quot;they are unneeded&quot; and try to convince PCs to join Hounds. Or at least throw Blood Talon alpha in to Death Rage on his packmates. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Any ideas on using Elodoth double agent in this scenario of Breaking Tribal Vows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}